# Phase 18B: keep Phase 18A benchmark evidence bundle byte-stable across
# platforms so its SHA-256 checksums verify on a fresh Windows checkout.
#
# `text eol=lf` is not strong enough on Windows when `core.autocrlf=true`
# is set globally (the working-tree files end up CRLF anyway). `binary`
# tells git to never transform these files: index bytes == working tree
# bytes == hashed bytes, on every platform. That is the only guarantee
# that lets the bundle's SHA-256 checksums verify on a fresh clone.
schemas/benchmarks/v1/*.schema.json binary
docs/runs/phase18a_benchmark_externalization_2026_05_05/export_bundle/**/*.json binary
docs/runs/phase18a_benchmark_externalization_2026_05_05/export_bundle/**/*.md binary
docs/runs/phase18a_benchmark_externalization_2026_05_05/export_bundle/checksums.sha256 binary
docs/runs/phase18a_benchmark_externalization_2026_05_05/export_bundle/README.md binary
